# AI and agent layer boundaries

## Durable Task Framework (DTF)

- **CI boundary:** **`Microsoft.DurableTask.*` must not appear** in **`ArchLucid.Application`** or **`ArchLucid.Contracts`** — see **`ArchLucid.Architecture.Tests/DtfNamespaceBoundaryArchitectureTests.cs`** (improvement #26).
- **Implementation posture:** DTF client/worker wiring, activities, and package references belong in **`ArchLucid.Host.Composition`** (and persistence adapters the orchestrator delegates to), not in agent runtime or domain libraries. Do not expand DTF into **`ArchLucid.Core`** or **`ArchLucid.AgentRuntime`** without an ADR and new architecture coverage.
- Authority runs: **`IAuthorityRunOrchestrator`** is the application port (**`ArchLucid.Application/Runs/Orchestration/IAuthorityRunOrchestrator.cs`**). Host composition registers legacy vs DTF-backed implementations; switching backends is configuration / DI, not a contract change on the port.

## Extension surfaces (prefer these over ad hoc services)

Use existing extension points; see **`.cursor/rules/Navigation.mdc`** for file-level entry points:

| Seam | Typical interface / area |
|------|---------------------------|
| Finding engines | **`IFindingEngine`** → **`ArchLucid.Decisioning`** registration |
| Context connectors | **`IContextConnector`**, **`IConnectorDescriptor`**, pipeline orchestration → **`ArchLucid.ContextIngestion`** |
| Agent handlers | **`IAgentHandler`** → **`ArchLucid.AgentRuntime`** + DI registration in host composition |
| Alert delivery | **`IAlertDeliveryChannel`** → **`ArchLucid.Decisioning/Alerts/Delivery`** |

New “agent-ish” behavior should plug into one of these patterns instead of duplicating orchestration in random feature classes.

## Logging and externally influenced strings

For LLM-adjacent and user-influenced identifiers in logs, follow **`.cursor/rules/CodeQL-Sanitized-Logging.mdc`** (**`ArchLucid.Core.Diagnostics`** sanitized extensions, **`docs/library/CODEQL_TRIAGE.md`**).

